rdhenry@ucrac1.ucr.edu (R. Dan Henry) writes:

>a lawful or chaotic individual would do may not be the same as
>another's. I don't expect every detail, but enough information to play

There is not very much difference that you should yourself worry about.
Some monsters are more probably peaceful to a certain alignment than
to the others, some artifacts can only be used by a certain alignment and
some other artifacts give you a blast if your alignment is "wrong" to use
it. But by the time you find artifacts, you probably can handle the first
time you pick it up or wield it, and if the blast seems too dangerous, 
don't touch it again. And you generally are asked first if you really
want to fight a peaceful monster..
The altars have an alignment, but you can always see the alignment once
you step on it. It seems easier to convert an altar to chaotic than to
other alignments.

I think about the only difference to specially remember is that only
chaotic characters can sacrifice humans or werecreatures without 
angering their god.
